==Projects==
===''[[The Fantastic Four: First Steps]]'' (2025)===
Set against the vibrant backdrop of a 1960s-inspired, [[Earth-828|retro-futuristic world]], "''The Fantastic Four: First Steps''" introduces Marvel's [[Fantastic Four|First Family]]—[[Mister Fantastic|Reed Richards/Mister Fantastic]] ([[Pedro Pascal]]), [[Invisible Woman|Sue Storm/Invisible Woman]] ([[Vanessa Kirby]]), [[Human Torch|Johnny Storm/Human Torch]] ([[Joseph Quinn]]), and [[Thing|Ben Grimm/The Thing]] ([[Ebon Moss-Bachrach]]) as they face their most daunting challenge yet. Forced to balance their roles as heroes with the strength of their family bond, they must defend [[Earth]] from a ravenous space god called [[Galactus]] ([[Ralph Ineson]]) and his enigmatic Herald, [[Silver Surfer]] ([[Julia Garner]]). And if Galactus' plan to devour the entire planet and everyone on it weren't bad enough, it suddenly gets [[Franklin Richards|very personal]].<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/thefantasticfourfirststeps/#!asset/gxpvc86gn362bnpv99hnxw FANTASTIC FOUR project profile FINAL 11-11-24.pdf]</ref>

===''[[Wonder Man (TV series)|Wonder Man]]'' (2026)===
====[[Wonder Man (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2026)====
Aspiring [[Hollywood]] actor [[Simon Williams]] is struggling to get his career off the ground. During a chance meeting with [[Trevor Slattery]], an actor whose biggest roles may be well behind him, Simon learns legendary director [[Von Kovak]] is remaking the superhero film "Wonder Man." These two actors at opposite ends of their careers doggedly pursue life-changing roles in this film as audiences get a peek behind the curtain of the entertainment industry.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/wonder-man/#!asset/6m6bq9m8cxhwwzmsscc3fbt6 WONDER MAN Project Profile.pdf]</ref>

===''[[Daredevil: Born Again]]'' (2025-TBA)===
====[[Daredevil: Born Again/Season Two|Season Two]] (2026)====
Mayor [[Wilson Fisk]] crushes [[New York City]] underfoot as he hunts down public enemy number one, the Hell's Kitchen vigilante known as [[Daredevil]]. But, beneath the horned mask, Matt Murdock will try to fight back from the shadows to tear down the Kingpin’s corrupt empire and redeem his home. Resist. Rebel. Rebuild.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/daredevil-born-again-season-2/#!asset/x7jhzwc75fj43bxnpx7jf79 Daredevil Born Again S2 Project Profile.pdf]</ref>

===''[[The Punisher: One Last Kill]]'' (2026)===
As [[Frank Castle]] searches for meaning beyond revenge, an unexpected force pulls him back into the fight.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess/#!asset/4ftbck4q6k4nhq5xq3th4p4 The Punisher One Last Kill Project Profile.pdf]</ref>

===''[[Spider-Man: Brand New Day]]'' (2026)===
It's a BRAND NEW DAY for [[Peter Parker]]. Fighting crime full-time as Spider-Man in a [[Earth|world]] that doesn’t remember him—and the pressure of seeing his [[Michelle Jones|old]] [[Ned Leeds|friends]] move on without him—sparks a change in Peter he may not have the power to control. But that transformation might also be the only thing that can stop a shocking new threat to the [[New York City|city]] and those he loves - a powerful villain no one can even see.

The world may have forgotten Peter Parker, but he hasn’t forgotten them.<ref>[https://spidermanbrandnewday.movie/synopsis/ Spider-Man Brand New Day Movie | Official Website | Sony Pictures]</ref>

